WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.253
Meet Kikumap: a mind map for your Claude chats, living in your Mac's menu bar.

2
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:16.816
One icon tells you what Claude is doing. The flower spins while a chat is running. A red badge counts the ones that finished, and an exclamation mark means Claude needs your approval.

3
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.061
When a chat finishes, it lights up on the map, so you always know where to look next.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.205
Your pinned chats become a map. Drag them onto your own topics, and the map makes room as you go.

5
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.904
Right-click any topic to give it a colour or a shape.

6
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:43.176
Tag your chats, like In progress, or Waiting on others. Click a tag to highlight everything that has it, or drag it straight onto a chat.

7
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:52.075
It's keyboard-first. Tab adds a subtopic, Return adds a sibling, Command arrow moves it, and Command Z undoes.

8
00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.680
Command F finds any topic, chat, or tag.

9
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:04.085
The timeline shows when Claude worked on what, and what's coming up next: your scheduled tasks, with live countdowns.

10
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.051
The menu sums up your day: which chats Claude worked on, and for how long.

11
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.328
Your plan usage is right there too, for this session and this week.

12
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:26.432
Export any topic: prompts, full conversations, artifacts, and a hand-off summary Claude writes. Import it into a new account, and pick up where you left off.

13
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.507
Or save the whole map as a PDF.

14
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.021
Your map is backed up every day, automatically.

15
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.027
Light or dark,

16
00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:40.891
in English, or Chinese.

17
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.275
Kikumap is free and open source. Get it on GitHub.

